slides.content:
# Multiple Classes and Dynamic Names

You can combine classes:

```jsx
<button className={`${styles.btn} ${styles.primary}`}>
```

Or use the `composes` keyword in CSS:

```css
/* Button.module.css */
.base {
  border-radius: 5px;
}
.primary {
  composes: base;
  background: blue;
}
```

You can also conditionally apply classes based on props.

slides.codeSnippet:
// components/Alert.module.css
.success { color: green; }
.error { color: red; }

// components/Alert.js
import styles from './Alert.module.css';

export default function Alert({ type, children }) {
  return <div className={styles[type]}>{children}</div>;
}
